+
+  // Clipping or top-left rasterization may leave no covered pixels. Test
+  // before alignment: rounding an empty interval outwards can create a tile
+  // that the guest never requested to copy or clear. The backend already
+  // handles zero extents as a successful no-op.
+  if (x0 >= x1 || y0 >= y1) {
+    return true;
+  }
+
+  // Direct3D 9's D3DDevice_Resolve internally rounds the right/bottom of the
+  // rectangle internally to 8. While all the alignment should have already been
+  // done by Direct3D 9, just for safety of host implementation of resolve,
